WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.549
Previously on Supernatural 22 years ago

00:00:02.584 --> 00:00:03.667
Sammy.

00:00:04.191 --> 00:00:06.081
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:06.116 --> 00:00:06.990
Go!

00:00:07.025 --> 00:00:09.544
Their mother Mysteriously died

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.982
Now two brothers...
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:12.017 --> 00:00:14.267
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:14.302 --> 00:00:16.518
Are on a quest to find their father

00:00:17.464 --> 00:00:18.498
This is dad's book.

00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:20.711
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:20.746 --> 00:00:22.762
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:22.797 --> 00:00:24.490
The family business.

00:00:24.652 --> 00:00:25.898
I got to find dad.

00:00:25.933 --> 00:00:28.472
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:47.222 --> 00:00:50.288
Where have you got those amp
up to? A hundred thousand volts.

00:00:50.438 --> 00:00:53.091
Damn. Yeah, I want this raw
head extra freaking crispy.

00:00:53.126 --> 00:00:55.745
Now, remember you only get
one shot with these things.

00:00:56.226 --> 00:00:58.188
So make it count.

00:01:30.989 --> 00:01:32.014
On three.

00:01:32.887 --> 00:01:33.955
One.

00:01:34.444 --> 00:01:35.762
Two.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.474
Three.

00:01:41.151 --> 00:01:42.738
Is it still here?

00:01:42.773 --> 00:01:43.888
Okay.

00:01:43.923 --> 00:01:45.803
Okay, hold your sister's hand.
We're gonna get you out of here.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:47.470
Let's go, let's go.

00:01:50.938 --> 00:01:52.491
All right, go!

00:01:55.231 --> 00:01:56.683
Sam!

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.480
Sam, get them out of here!

00:02:04.515 --> 00:02:05.860
Here, take this!

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.235
Run!

00:02:17.255 --> 00:02:19.663
Come on!

00:02:57.972 --> 00:02:59.491
Dean!

00:03:00.268 --> 00:03:01.147
Dean!

00:03:01.368 --> 00:03:02.256
Hey!

00:03:02.693 --> 00:03:04.599
Hey, hey!

00:03:14.211 --> 00:03:15.742
Sorry, I'm so sorry to ask.

00:03:15.777 --> 00:03:18.115
There doesn't seem to
be any insurance on file.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:20.157
Right, um...

00:03:21.869 --> 00:03:23.405
Okay.

00:03:24.865 --> 00:03:28.176
Okay, Mr. Burkevits.

00:03:30.649 --> 00:03:34.279
Look, we can finish this
up later. No, no it's okay.

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:37.286
We were just taking a short cut
through the neighborhood and um...

00:03:37.321 --> 00:03:40.073
Windows were all down,
we heard some screaming.

00:03:40.108 --> 00:03:42.826
We drove pass the house
and we stopped, ran in.

00:03:42.861 --> 00:03:44.356
And you found the kids in the basement.

00:03:44.391 --> 00:03:45.227
Yeah.

00:03:45.262 --> 00:03:47.508
Well, thank god you did.

00:03:47.917 --> 00:03:51.045
Excuse me. Sure, thanks for your help.

00:03:51.311 --> 00:03:52.256
Hey, doc. Is he...

00:03:52.291 --> 00:03:54.428
He's resting. And?

00:03:54.463 --> 00:03:56.953
The electrocution
triggered a heart attack.

00:03:56.988 --> 00:04:01.709
A pretty massive one. I'm
afraid his heart, it's damaged.

00:04:01.744 --> 00:04:04.386
How damaged? We've done all we can.

00:04:04.421 --> 00:04:07.643
We can try and keep him
comfortable at this point but...

00:04:07.678 --> 00:04:10.866
I'll give him a couple of
weeks at most, maybe a month.

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:12.397
No, no, there is...

00:04:12.432 --> 00:04:15.278
There's gotta be something you
can do. Some kind of treatment.

00:04:15.313 --> 00:04:17.522
We can't work miracles.

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:20.200
I really am sorry.

00:04:29.489 --> 00:04:35.107
You ever actually watched
daytime TV? It's terrible.

00:04:36.757 --> 00:04:38.342
I talked to your doctor.

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.790
That fabric soft teddy bear, oh.

00:04:40.825 --> 00:04:43.699
I'll hunt that bitch down. Dean...

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:45.947
Yeah.

00:04:45.982 --> 00:04:49.743
All right, well. Looks like
you're gonna leave town without me.

00:04:49.778 --> 00:04:51.808
What are you talking about?
I'm not gonna leave you here.

00:04:51.843 --> 00:04:53.713
Hey, if you take care of that car.

00:04:53.748 --> 00:04:55.549
I'll swear I'll hunt your ass.

00:04:55.584 --> 00:04:59.551
I don't think that's funny. Uh,
come on. It's a little funny.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:09.528
Look, Sam. What can I say,
man. It's a dangerous gig.

00:05:09.563 --> 00:05:11.976
I drew the short straw.
That it, end of story.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.254
Don't talk like that, all right?

00:05:14.289 --> 00:05:17.256
We still have options. What options?

00:05:17.291 --> 00:05:20.154
Get burial or cremation?

00:05:20.189 --> 00:05:23.017
I know it's not easy.

00:05:24.165 --> 00:05:26.788
But I'm gonna die.

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:29.702
And you can't stop it.

00:05:31.695 --> 00:05:33.436
Watch me.

00:05:33.471 --> 00:05:35.935
This is John Winchester.
I can't be reached.

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:38.399
If this is an emergency
call my son Dean.

00:05:38.434 --> 00:05:43.702
866-907-3235.
He can help.

00:05:43.737 --> 00:05:46.474
Hey, dad. It's Sam.

00:05:47.745 --> 00:05:50.111
You probably won't get this but uh...

00:05:50.146 --> 00:05:52.064
It's Dean...

00:05:52.099 --> 00:05:54.803
He's sick and uh...

00:05:54.967 --> 00:05:58.588
Doctors says there
nothing they can do. Um...

00:05:59.874 --> 00:06:01.260
But uh...

00:06:01.295 --> 00:06:04.278
They don't know things
we know, right? Um...

00:06:04.313 --> 00:06:06.942
So, don't worry, cause I'm uh...

00:06:06.977 --> 00:06:10.066
Gonna do everything it
takes to get him better.

00:06:10.982 --> 00:06:12.460
All right.

00:06:12.495 --> 00:06:14.868
Just wanted you to know.

00:06:29.482 --> 00:06:30.811
What the hell are you doing here?

00:06:30.846 --> 00:06:33.818
I checked myself out. Are you crazy?

00:06:33.853 --> 00:06:37.896
I'm not gonna die in a hospital
where the nurses aren't even hot.

00:06:38.139 --> 00:06:40.407
You know, this whole...

00:06:40.442 --> 00:06:42.874
I laugh in the face of
death thing... It's crap.

00:06:42.909 --> 00:06:45.199
I can see right through it.

00:06:45.234 --> 00:06:47.158
Yeah, whatever dude.

00:06:47.193 --> 00:06:49.389
Have you even slept?
You look worse than me.

00:06:49.424 --> 00:06:53.160
I've been scattering the
internet for the last three days.

00:06:54.737 --> 00:06:57.780
Calling every contact
in dad journal. For what?

00:06:57.815 --> 00:06:59.608
For what'll help you.

00:06:59.643 --> 00:07:02.699
One of dad's friends
Joshua. He called me back.

00:07:02.734 --> 00:07:05.271
Told me about a guy in
Nebraska. Specialist.

00:07:05.306 --> 00:07:07.808
You're not gonna let me
die in peace, are you?

00:07:07.843 --> 00:07:09.861
I'm not gonna let you die, period.

00:07:09.896 --> 00:07:12.380
We're going.

00:07:32.525 --> 00:07:35.642
The church of Roy Le Grange
Faith Healer. Witness the miracle

00:07:36.945 --> 00:07:39.899
I got you. I got it!

00:07:40.824 --> 00:07:42.756
Man, you're a lying bastard.

00:07:42.791 --> 00:07:44.855
I thought you said we
were going to see a doctor.

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:46.578
I believe I said a 'specialist'.

00:07:46.613 --> 00:07:48.852
Look Dean, this guy's
suppose to be the real deal.

00:07:48.887 --> 00:07:52.322
I can't believe you brought me here to see
some guy who heals people out of a tent!

00:07:52.357 --> 00:07:55.336
Reverend Le Grange is a
great man. Yeah, that's nice.

00:07:55.371 --> 00:07:57.591
I have a right to protest.
This man is a fraud.

00:07:57.626 --> 00:08:00.074
He's bilking all these people
out of their hard earned money!

00:08:00.109 --> 00:08:03.513
This is a place of
worship. Let's go, move it.

00:08:03.548 --> 00:08:05.755
I take it he's not part of the flock.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:08.176
What would people see something
that they can't explain.

00:08:08.211 --> 00:08:10.563
There's controversy. Come
on, Sam. A Faith Healer?

00:08:10.598 --> 00:08:13.913
Maybe it's time to have
a little faith Dean.

00:08:14.666 --> 00:08:16.733
You know what I got faith in? Reality.

00:08:16.768 --> 00:08:18.966
Knowing what's really going on.

00:08:19.001 --> 00:08:20.548
How can you be a skeptic?

00:08:20.583 --> 00:08:22.010
With the things we see everyday.

00:08:22.045 --> 00:08:24.021
Exactly, we see them.
We know they're real.

00:08:24.056 --> 00:08:25.319
But if you know evil's out there

00:08:25.354 --> 00:08:26.920
How can you not believe
good's out there too?

00:08:26.955 --> 00:08:28.486
Cause I've seen what
evil does to good people.

00:08:28.521 --> 00:08:31.307
Maybe god works in mysterious ways.

00:08:31.868 --> 00:08:33.950
Maybe he does.

00:08:33.985 --> 00:08:36.265
I think you just turned
me Around on the subject.

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.349
Yeah, I'm sure.

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:40.477
I'm Dean. This is Sam.

00:08:40.512 --> 00:08:42.249
Leila.

00:08:42.284 --> 00:08:45.645
Sir, if you're not a believer
then why are you here?

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:49.156
Well, apparently my brother here
believes enough for the both of us.

00:08:49.191 --> 00:08:52.446
Come on Leila. It's
about to start. All right.

00:08:52.481 --> 00:08:54.216
Bye.

00:08:54.483 --> 00:08:57.433
Well, I bet you, she can
work in mysterious ways.

00:08:57.468 --> 00:08:59.561
Ladies and gentlemen, please be seated.

00:08:59.596 --> 00:09:02.889
We're starting in just a moment.
Welcome all faiths True believers revival

00:09:05.204 --> 00:09:08.506
Yeah, peace love and trust all over.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:14.222
Come on.

00:09:14.257 --> 00:09:15.561
Don't, we're sitting here.

00:09:15.596 --> 00:09:16.998
We're sitting up front.

00:09:17.033 --> 00:09:18.400
What? Why? Come on.

00:09:18.435 --> 00:09:19.927
Oh, come on Sam.

00:09:19.962 --> 00:09:21.384
You're all right?

00:09:21.419 --> 00:09:25.086
This is ridiculous. I'm
good, dude. Get off me.

00:09:26.113 --> 00:09:28.096
Perfect. Yeah, perfect.

00:09:28.131 --> 00:09:30.064
Take it off

00:09:39.786 --> 00:09:44.388
Each morning my wife Sue
Ann brings me the news.

00:09:44.423 --> 00:09:46.939
Never seems good, does it? No.

00:09:46.974 --> 00:09:49.421
Seems like there's always someone

00:09:49.456 --> 00:09:54.863
Committing some immoral,
unspeakable act. That's right.

00:09:54.898 --> 00:09:57.989
But I say to you. God is watching.

00:09:58.024 --> 00:09:59.434
Here, here.

00:09:59.469 --> 00:10:05.987
God rewards the good and he
punishes the corrupt. Right.

00:10:06.022 --> 00:10:10.614
It is the Lord who does
the healing here friends.

00:10:10.649 --> 00:10:15.172
The Lord who guides me
and chosen who to heal

00:10:15.207 --> 00:10:18.788
By helping me to see into
people's hearts. Amen.

00:10:18.823 --> 00:10:21.233
Yeah, rid of their wallets.

00:10:21.268 --> 00:10:23.643
You think so young man?

00:10:25.084 --> 00:10:28.503
Sorry. No, no. Don't be.

00:10:28.538 --> 00:10:33.479
Just watch what you say around a
blind man. We got real sharp ears.

00:10:34.535 --> 00:10:36.929
What's your name son?

00:10:37.567 --> 00:10:40.342
Dean. Dean.

00:10:42.083 --> 00:10:45.871
I want you to come up here with me.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:55.402
No, it's okay.

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:56.690
What are you doing?

00:10:56.725 --> 00:11:00.618
You come here to be healed, haven't you?

00:11:02.829 --> 00:11:05.647
Oh, yeah but uh...

00:11:05.682 --> 00:11:09.623
Maybe you should just pick someone else.

00:11:12.123 --> 00:11:16.743
I didn't pick you Dean. The Lord did.

00:11:18.224 --> 00:11:20.622
Get up there!

00:11:20.851 --> 00:11:24.994
Yes. Yes. Amen.

00:11:31.236 --> 00:11:32.962
You're ready?

00:11:32.997 --> 00:11:35.800
Yeah, with no disrespect but uh...

00:11:35.835 --> 00:11:38.623
I'm not exactly a believer.

00:11:38.768 --> 00:11:40.653
You will be son.

00:11:40.688 --> 00:11:42.538
You will be.

00:11:42.722 --> 00:11:45.396
Pray with me friends.

00:12:09.068 --> 00:12:13.260
All right now.

00:12:22.258 --> 00:12:24.862
All right now.

00:12:29.311 --> 00:12:31.028
Dean!

00:12:35.885 --> 00:12:37.925
Say something!

00:12:51.256 --> 00:12:53.111
So you really feel okay?

00:12:53.146 --> 00:12:54.464
I feel fine Sam.

00:12:54.499 --> 00:12:58.361
Well, according to all your tests.
There's nothing wrong with your heart.

00:12:58.396 --> 00:13:00.121
No sign there ever was.

00:13:00.156 --> 00:13:03.888
Not that a man your age should
be having heart trouble but uh...

00:13:03.923 --> 00:13:05.902
Still it's strange, it does happen.

00:13:05.937 --> 00:13:07.063
What do you mean strange?

00:13:07.098 --> 00:13:10.711
Well, just yesterday a young
guy like you. 27, athletic.

00:13:10.746 --> 00:13:13.414
I don't know a heart attack.

00:13:14.255 --> 00:13:16.053
Thanks doc.

00:13:16.088 --> 00:13:17.851
No problem.

00:13:19.006 --> 00:13:21.112
That's odd. Maybe it's coincidence.

00:13:21.147 --> 00:13:23.267
People's heart give up all
the time, man. No they don't.

00:13:23.302 --> 00:13:25.352
Look Dean. Do we really have
to look this one in the mouth?

00:13:25.387 --> 00:13:28.021
Why can't we just be thankful that
the guy saved your life and move on?

00:13:28.056 --> 00:13:30.787
Because I can't shake
this feeling, that's why.

00:13:30.822 --> 00:13:32.739
What feeling?

00:13:32.774 --> 00:13:36.204
When I was healed. I just, I felt wrong.

00:13:36.239 --> 00:13:39.510
Felt cold and for a second

00:13:39.545 --> 00:13:41.429
I saw someone. I saw this old man.

00:13:41.464 --> 00:13:43.278
I'm telling you Sam. It was a spirit.

00:13:43.313 --> 00:13:45.922
But if there was something there
Dean. I think I would have seen it too.

00:13:45.957 --> 00:13:48.150
I mean I've been seeing
awful lot of things lately.

00:13:48.185 --> 00:13:49.899
Well, excuse me psychic wonder.

00:13:49.934 --> 00:13:52.865
But you just need a
little faith on this one.

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:57.042
Sam, I've been hunting long enough
to trust a feeling like this.

00:13:59.347 --> 00:14:01.334
Yeah, right.

00:14:02.406 --> 00:14:04.649
So what do you want to do?

00:14:04.684 --> 00:14:06.061
Why don't you to check
out that heart attack guy.

00:14:06.096 --> 00:14:08.292
I'm gonna visit the reverend.

00:14:11.221 --> 00:14:12.814
I feel great.

00:14:12.849 --> 00:14:14.372
Just trying to...

00:14:14.407 --> 00:14:16.488
You know, make sense of what happened.

00:14:16.523 --> 00:14:19.415
A miracle's what happened.

00:14:19.794 --> 00:14:24.321
Miracles come so often around Roy.

00:14:25.014 --> 00:14:27.623
When did they start? The miracles.

00:14:27.658 --> 00:14:30.197
Woke up one morning stone blind.

00:14:30.232 --> 00:14:34.564
Doctors figured out I had cancer.
Told me I had maybe a month.

00:14:34.599 --> 00:14:36.157
So uh...

00:14:36.192 --> 00:14:38.448
We prayed for a miracle.

00:14:38.483 --> 00:14:41.063
I was weak but...

00:14:41.098 --> 00:14:44.492
I told Sue Ann to just keep on praying.

00:14:44.527 --> 00:14:46.064
I went into a coma.

00:14:46.099 --> 00:14:48.898
Doctors said I wouldn't
wake up but I did.

00:14:48.933 --> 00:14:51.398
And the cancer was gone.

00:14:51.433 --> 00:14:57.095
If it wasn't for these eyes, no
one would believe I ever had it.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.804
And suddenly you can heal people?

00:14:59.839 --> 00:15:02.412
I discovered it afterwards, yes.

00:15:02.447 --> 00:15:04.950
God's blessed me in many ways.

00:15:04.985 --> 00:15:10.520
And his flock swelled over night.
And this is just the beginning.

00:15:12.156 --> 00:15:14.372
Can I ask you one last question?

00:15:14.407 --> 00:15:16.641
Of course you can.

00:15:17.333 --> 00:15:19.893
Why? Why me?

00:15:19.928 --> 00:15:23.279
Out of all the sick people why save me?

00:15:23.314 --> 00:15:27.090
Well, like I said before.
The Lord guides me.

00:15:27.125 --> 00:15:34.541
I looked into your heart and you
just stood out from all the rest.

00:15:34.705 --> 00:15:38.332
What did you see in my heart?

00:15:38.367 --> 00:15:42.126
A young man with an important
purpose. A job to do.

00:15:42.161 --> 00:15:45.183
And it isn't finished.

00:15:46.908 --> 00:15:51.003
He seemed healthy. Swam
everyday. Didn't smoke.

00:15:51.038 --> 00:15:53.899
It's no so hard to act this
kind of scene. No bizarre.

00:15:53.934 --> 00:15:56.760
And you said he was running?
Right before he collapsed?

00:15:56.795 --> 00:15:58.672
Yeah, yeah. He was freaking out.

00:15:58.707 --> 00:16:00.418
Said that something was...

00:16:00.453 --> 00:16:02.095
After him. Did he say what?

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:05.783
Thin air, that's what. I
mean, there wasn't anything.

00:16:05.967 --> 00:16:07.854
All right, thanks.

00:16:10.309 --> 00:16:11.783
Hey buddy. You're...

00:16:11.818 --> 00:16:13.291
You're clock's busted.

00:16:13.326 --> 00:16:14.730
Oh, yeah. We uh...

00:16:14.765 --> 00:16:19.236
We can't get it working.
Just froze at 4:17.

00:16:19.271 --> 00:16:21.839
Is that the same time Marshall died?

00:16:21.874 --> 00:16:23.731
How did you know?

00:16:27.209 --> 00:16:29.756
Dean, hey. Hey.

00:16:29.953 --> 00:16:31.659
How you feeling? I feel good.

00:16:31.694 --> 00:16:34.091
Cured, I guess.

00:16:34.126 --> 00:16:35.689
What are you doing here?

00:16:35.724 --> 00:16:38.953
You know my mom. She wanted
to talk to the reverend.

00:16:38.988 --> 00:16:40.704
Leila.

00:16:41.738 --> 00:16:45.858
Yes, we're here again. Oh,
I'm sorry but Roy's resting.

00:16:45.893 --> 00:16:48.284
He won't be seeing anyone right now.

00:16:48.319 --> 00:16:50.320
Sue Ann please.

00:16:50.355 --> 00:16:52.998
This is our sixth time.
He's got to see us.

00:16:53.033 --> 00:16:55.213
Roy is aware of Leila's situation

00:16:55.248 --> 00:16:58.367
And he very well much wants to help
just as soon as the Lord allows.

00:16:58.402 --> 00:17:01.694
Have faith Mrs. Roke.

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:11.413
Why are you still even here?

00:17:11.448 --> 00:17:13.502
You've got what you wanted. Mom.

00:17:13.537 --> 00:17:15.365
Stop.

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:17.976
No Leila this is too much.

00:17:18.011 --> 00:17:20.491
We've been to every single service.

00:17:20.526 --> 00:17:23.441
If Roy would stop choosing
these strangers over you.

00:17:23.476 --> 00:17:26.639
Strangers who don't even believe.

00:17:26.674 --> 00:17:29.802
I just can't pray any harder.

00:17:29.837 --> 00:17:32.448
Leila, what's wrong?

00:17:34.652 --> 00:17:36.944
I have this thing.

00:17:36.979 --> 00:17:39.236
It's a brain tumor.

00:17:39.691 --> 00:17:42.636
It's inoperable.

00:17:42.812 --> 00:17:46.547
In sixth months the doctors say...

00:17:50.982 --> 00:17:53.217
I'm sorry.

00:17:53.751 --> 00:17:55.651
It's okay.

00:17:55.686 --> 00:17:57.666
No.

00:17:57.952 --> 00:18:00.667
It isn't.

00:18:05.865 --> 00:18:10.278
Why do you deserve to
live more than my daughter?

00:18:38.652 --> 00:18:40.991
What did you find out?

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.631
I'm sorry.

00:18:43.819 --> 00:18:45.010
Sorry about what?

00:18:45.045 --> 00:18:50.579
Marshall Hall died at 4:17.

00:18:50.797 --> 00:18:53.285
The exact time I was healed. Yeah.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:56.863
So, I put together a list.
Everyone Roy's healed.

00:18:56.898 --> 00:19:00.509
Six people over the past year and I
cross checked them with local obits.

00:19:00.544 --> 00:19:03.245
Every time someone was
healed someone else died.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:04.666
And each time the victim died

00:19:04.701 --> 00:19:07.572
Of the same symptom Le Grange
was healing at the time.

00:19:07.607 --> 00:19:10.443
Someone healed a cancer,
someone else died of cancer?

00:19:10.478 --> 00:19:13.849
Somehow. Le Grange...

00:19:14.033 --> 00:19:18.226
Is trading a life for another. Hello?

00:19:19.397 --> 00:19:21.101
Wait, wait, wait. So...

00:19:21.136 --> 00:19:23.713
Marshall Hall died to save me?

00:19:23.748 --> 00:19:25.642
Dean...

00:19:25.856 --> 00:19:28.282
The guy probably would have died anyway.

00:19:28.317 --> 00:19:30.708
And someone else would have been healed.

00:19:32.862 --> 00:19:35.230
You never should have brought me here.

00:19:35.265 --> 00:19:37.814
Dean, I was just trying
to save your life.

00:19:37.849 --> 00:19:40.363
But Sam, some guy is
dead now because of me!

00:19:40.398 --> 00:19:43.172
I didn't know.

00:19:44.008 --> 00:19:47.015
Pray with me friends.

00:19:47.857 --> 00:19:51.046
The thing I don't understand
is how is Roy doing it?

00:19:51.081 --> 00:19:53.892
How's he trading a life for a life?

00:19:53.927 --> 00:19:56.674
Oh, he's not doing it.

00:19:56.819 --> 00:19:58.949
Something else is doing it for him.

00:19:58.984 --> 00:20:03.268
What do you mean? The
old man I saw on stage.

00:20:03.658 --> 00:20:05.456
I didn't want to believe
it. But deep down, I knew it.

00:20:05.491 --> 00:20:07.549
You knew what? What
are you talking about?

00:20:07.584 --> 00:20:11.946
There's only one thing that can
give and take life like that.

00:20:11.981 --> 00:20:14.613
We're dealing with a reaper.

00:21:14.521 --> 00:21:16.282
You really think it's the 'Grim Reaper'?

00:21:16.317 --> 00:21:19.303
Like Angel of Death, the
Collector of Soul the whole deal?

00:21:19.338 --> 00:21:21.829
No, no, no. Not 'The
Reaper'. A 'Reaper'.

00:21:21.864 --> 00:21:24.180
There's reaper law in pretty
much every culture on earth.

00:21:24.215 --> 00:21:25.949
They go by a hundred different names.

00:21:25.984 --> 00:21:27.932
It's possible this one's one of them.

00:21:27.967 --> 00:21:29.845
But you said you saw a dude in a suit.

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:33.845
What? You think he should be
working the whole black robe thing?

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:36.731
You said it yourself that
the clock stopped right?

00:21:37.635 --> 00:21:39.669
Reapers stop time.

00:21:39.704 --> 00:21:41.190
And you can only see them
when they're coming at you

00:21:41.225 --> 00:21:43.247
Which is why I could
see him and you couldn't.

00:21:43.282 --> 00:21:45.234
Maybe. There's nothing
else that could be Sam.

00:21:45.269 --> 00:21:48.499
The question is how's Roy
controlling the damn thing.

00:21:48.534 --> 00:21:50.190
That cross.

00:21:50.225 --> 00:21:52.624
What? There was this cross.

00:21:52.659 --> 00:21:57.236
I noticed it in the church
tent, I knew I seen it before.

00:22:02.961 --> 00:22:04.812
Here.

00:22:05.356 --> 00:22:06.461
Tarot?

00:22:06.496 --> 00:22:08.046
It makes sense.

00:22:08.081 --> 00:22:10.232
I mean, tarot dates back to
the early Christian, right?

00:22:10.267 --> 00:22:11.998
When some priests
were still using magic?

00:22:12.033 --> 00:22:13.694
And a few of them viewed
into the dark stuff.

00:22:13.729 --> 00:22:17.905
Necromancy and how to push
death away, how to cause it.

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:20.791
So Roy's using black
magic to bind the reaper.

00:22:20.826 --> 00:22:22.986
If he is, he's riding the whirlwind.

00:22:23.021 --> 00:22:26.942
It's like putting a dog
leash on a great white.

00:22:33.083 --> 00:22:35.826
Okay, then we stop Roy. How?

00:22:35.861 --> 00:22:36.831
You know how?

00:22:36.866 --> 00:22:38.265
Wait, what the hell are
you talking about Dean?

00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:40.113
We can't kill Roy.

00:22:40.148 --> 00:22:41.301
Sam. The guy's playing god.

00:22:41.336 --> 00:22:43.953
He's deciding who lives and who
dies. That's a monster in my books.

00:22:43.988 --> 00:22:46.853
No, we're not gonna
kill a human being Dean.

00:22:46.888 --> 00:22:48.782
We do that, we're no better than he is.

00:22:48.817 --> 00:22:51.601
Okay, so we can't kill
Roy. We can't kill death.

00:22:51.636 --> 00:22:54.684
Any bright ideas college boy?

00:22:54.975 --> 00:22:56.306
Okay, uh...

00:22:56.341 --> 00:22:58.721
If Roy's using some kind
of black spell on the reaper

00:22:58.756 --> 00:23:01.149
We gotta figure out what it is.

00:23:01.184 --> 00:23:03.713
And how to break it.

00:23:08.799 --> 00:23:12.025
Service today.

00:23:16.777 --> 00:23:19.415
If Roy's using a spell.
There might be a spell book.

00:23:19.450 --> 00:23:20.617
See if you can find it.

00:23:20.652 --> 00:23:23.481
Hurry up. Services start in 15
minutes. I'll try to stroll Roy.

00:23:23.516 --> 00:23:26.259
All right. Le Grange is
a fraud. He's no healer.

00:23:26.294 --> 00:23:27.961
Amen, brother. You
keep up the good work.

00:23:27.996 --> 00:23:29.650
Thank you.

00:24:26.478 --> 00:24:28.770
Encyclopedia of Christian
History Old & New Testament

00:24:55.334 --> 00:25:00.934
Openly gay teacher wins lawsuit
Strong message sent to Nations...

00:25:11.058 --> 00:25:14.316
Wright: 'local church a cult'

00:25:23.843 --> 00:25:24.726
What have you got?

00:25:24.761 --> 00:25:26.751
Roy's choosing victims
he sees as a immoral.

00:25:26.786 --> 00:25:28.706
And I think I know
who's next on his list.

00:25:28.741 --> 00:25:30.755
Remember the protestor?
The guy in the parking lot?

00:25:30.790 --> 00:25:32.814
Yeah. Yeah, I'll find him.

00:25:32.849 --> 00:25:35.795
But you can't let Roy
heal anyone, all right?

00:25:56.410 --> 00:25:57.346
Leila.

00:25:57.381 --> 00:26:00.606
Leila Roke, come up here child.

00:26:05.896 --> 00:26:07.898
Mom... Baby.

00:26:07.933 --> 00:26:09.900
I love you.

00:26:10.950 --> 00:26:13.042
Oh, man.

00:26:22.169 --> 00:26:24.846
Leila, listen to me.
You can't get up there.

00:26:24.881 --> 00:26:26.824
Why not? We've waited for months.

00:26:26.859 --> 00:26:28.623
You can't let Roy heal you.

00:26:28.658 --> 00:26:30.671
I don't understand. Roy
healed you, didn't he?

00:26:30.706 --> 00:26:32.649
I mean, why wouldn't
you at least let him try?

00:26:32.684 --> 00:26:35.890
Because if you do, something
bad is going to happen.

00:26:35.925 --> 00:26:39.096
I can't explain. I just need
you to believe me. Leila.

00:26:39.131 --> 00:26:41.295
Please...

00:26:49.560 --> 00:26:50.972
I'm sorry.

00:26:51.007 --> 00:26:52.875
Leila. Leila!

00:26:52.910 --> 00:26:54.743
Dear child.

00:26:55.834 --> 00:26:59.019
You deserve this. I knew
the Lord would reply me...

00:26:59.054 --> 00:27:01.952
I knew the Lord would reply me.

00:27:05.421 --> 00:27:07.286
Help!

00:27:14.366 --> 00:27:16.717
Pray with me friends.

00:27:20.804 --> 00:27:23.889
I hope you're ready. I am.

00:27:34.165 --> 00:27:35.506
Help!

00:27:35.541 --> 00:27:36.899
Help me please!

00:27:36.934 --> 00:27:38.257
Where is it?

00:27:38.472 --> 00:27:40.724
It's right there!

00:27:42.157 --> 00:27:44.169
Come on, come on.

00:27:52.920 --> 00:27:54.390
Fire!

00:27:54.425 --> 00:27:56.996
The tent's on fire!

00:27:57.144 --> 00:27:59.131
Fire! Everybody get out of here!

00:27:59.166 --> 00:28:01.716
Roy! Roy, please!

00:28:01.751 --> 00:28:03.864
Please don't stop. Please!

00:28:03.899 --> 00:28:05.840
Reverend, please!

00:28:05.875 --> 00:28:07.781
Please don't stop.

00:28:07.816 --> 00:28:09.400
Please.

00:28:09.435 --> 00:28:10.950
Friends.

00:28:10.985 --> 00:28:14.561
If you all just leave the tent
in an orderly fashion and...

00:28:14.596 --> 00:28:17.269
We'll figure out what's
going on out there and...

00:28:17.304 --> 00:28:20.161
I did it. I stopped Roy.

00:28:20.196 --> 00:28:23.018
David? I think its okay.

00:28:26.768 --> 00:28:28.378
No!

00:28:28.413 --> 00:28:29.605
Dean, it didn't work!

00:28:29.640 --> 00:28:31.626
The reaper's still coming!

00:28:32.600 --> 00:28:34.143
I'm telling you... I'm telling you.

00:28:34.178 --> 00:28:36.777
It must not have worked! Roy must
not be controlling this thing!

00:28:36.812 --> 00:28:39.305
Then who the hell is?

00:28:42.356 --> 00:28:44.469
Sue Ann.

00:28:58.611 --> 00:29:00.903
Help! Help me!

00:29:01.047 --> 00:29:02.837
Help!

00:29:17.268 --> 00:29:19.591
I got you. I got you.

00:29:22.134 --> 00:29:24.118
Thank god.

00:29:29.398 --> 00:29:32.433
I just don't understand.

00:29:32.468 --> 00:29:34.231
After everything we have done for you.

00:29:34.266 --> 00:29:37.358
After Roy healed you.

00:29:38.312 --> 00:29:42.658
I'm just very very disappointed Dean.

00:29:43.994 --> 00:29:46.467
You can let him go. I'm
not gonna press charges.

00:29:46.502 --> 00:29:51.656
The Lord will deal
with him as he sees fit.

00:29:53.401 --> 00:29:54.976
We catch you around here again son.

00:29:55.011 --> 00:29:57.727
Who put the fear god in you, understand?

00:29:57.762 --> 00:29:59.494
Yes, sir. Fear god.

00:29:59.529 --> 00:30:01.348
Got it.

00:30:04.400 --> 00:30:05.932
Leila.

00:30:06.621 --> 00:30:08.244
Why would you do that Dean?

00:30:08.279 --> 00:30:10.574
It could have been my only chance.

00:30:10.609 --> 00:30:12.551
He's not a healer.

00:30:12.586 --> 00:30:14.493
He healed you.

00:30:16.131 --> 00:30:18.174
I know it doesn't seem fair.

00:30:18.209 --> 00:30:22.808
And I wish I could explain. But
Roy's not the answer, I'm sorry.

00:30:24.787 --> 00:30:27.293
Goodbye Dean.

00:30:31.870 --> 00:30:35.839
I wish you luck. I really do.

00:30:35.874 --> 00:30:38.451
Same to you.

00:30:42.427 --> 00:30:45.721
You deserve it a lot more than me.

00:30:49.074 --> 00:30:51.539
Private session tonight.
No interruptions.

00:30:51.574 --> 00:30:54.004
I give you my word.
I'll heal your daughter.

00:30:54.039 --> 00:30:57.530
Thank you, reverend. God bless you.

00:31:01.640 --> 00:31:04.913
So Roy really believes.

00:31:05.452 --> 00:31:08.101
I don't think he has any
idea what his wife's doing.

00:31:08.136 --> 00:31:12.308
Well, I found this
Hidden in their library.

00:31:12.343 --> 00:31:15.604
It's ancient. Written by a
priest who went dark side.

00:31:15.639 --> 00:31:17.678
There's a binding spell in here.

00:31:17.713 --> 00:31:19.502
For trapping a reaper.

00:31:19.537 --> 00:31:21.889
Must be hell of a spell. Yeah.

00:31:21.924 --> 00:31:25.148
You got to build a black altar
with seriously dark stuff.

00:31:25.183 --> 00:31:28.637
Bones. Human blood.

00:31:28.672 --> 00:31:32.132
To cross a line like
that. That preacher's wife.

00:31:32.167 --> 00:31:36.676
Black magic, murder, evil.

00:31:36.711 --> 00:31:38.480
Desperate.

00:31:38.515 --> 00:31:41.788
Her husband was dying. She would
have done anything to save him.

00:31:41.823 --> 00:31:45.061
She was using the binding spell
to keep the reaper away from Roy.

00:31:45.096 --> 00:31:48.701
Cheating death. Literally.

00:31:48.736 --> 00:31:52.110
Yeah, but Roy's alive so why
is she still using the spell?

00:31:52.145 --> 00:31:57.651
Right. To force the reaper to help
the people she thinks are moral.

00:31:58.655 --> 00:32:02.116
Thank god save us from half the people
who think they're doing god's work.

00:32:02.151 --> 00:32:05.714
We got to break that binding spell Dean.

00:32:07.928 --> 00:32:10.325
You know Sue Ann had to
cop a cross like this.

00:32:10.360 --> 00:32:12.687
And when she dropped it
the reaper backed off.

00:32:12.722 --> 00:32:15.599
So you think we got to find
the cross or destroy the altar.

00:32:15.634 --> 00:32:17.578
Maybe both?

00:32:18.610 --> 00:32:21.025
Whatever we do. We'd
better to do it soon.

00:32:21.060 --> 00:32:24.021
Roy's healing Leila tonight.

00:32:35.866 --> 00:32:37.742
That's Leila's car.

00:32:37.777 --> 00:32:39.618
She's already here.

00:32:39.653 --> 00:32:41.405
Yeah.

00:32:42.166 --> 00:32:44.907
Dean. You know, if Roy would
have picked Leila instead of me.

00:32:44.942 --> 00:32:47.067
She'd be healed by now. Dean, don't.

00:32:47.102 --> 00:32:49.385
And if she's not healed tonight...

00:32:49.420 --> 00:32:51.813
She's gonna die in a couple of months.

00:32:51.848 --> 00:32:54.172
What's happening to her is horrible.

00:32:54.207 --> 00:32:58.518
But what are you going to do?
Let somebody else die to save her?

00:32:58.553 --> 00:33:03.183
You said it yourself
Dean. You can't play god.

00:33:17.034 --> 00:33:18.071
Gather around.

00:33:18.106 --> 00:33:20.259
Please, everyone gather around.

00:33:20.294 --> 00:33:22.412
Come in closer. Come on up.

00:33:22.447 --> 00:33:24.704
Where's Sue Ann?

00:33:25.129 --> 00:33:27.144
House.

00:33:27.956 --> 00:33:29.464
Go find Sue Ann. I'll catch up.

00:33:29.499 --> 00:33:30.981
What are you...

00:33:32.363 --> 00:33:34.013
Hey.

00:33:34.723 --> 00:33:38.099
You're gonna put that fear god in me?

00:34:21.751 --> 00:34:23.534
See him?

00:34:23.858 --> 00:34:25.692
Na.

00:34:46.661 --> 00:34:49.086
Psycho mutt.

00:35:34.433 --> 00:35:38.579
I gave your brother a life
and I can take it away.

00:35:50.132 --> 00:35:52.042
Sam, can't you see?

00:35:52.077 --> 00:35:53.917
The Lord chose me.

00:35:53.952 --> 00:35:56.687
The reward the just
and punish the wicked.

00:35:56.722 --> 00:35:59.070
And your brother is wicked.

00:35:59.105 --> 00:36:03.485
And he deserves to die just
as Leila deserves to live.

00:36:03.520 --> 00:36:06.219
That's god's will.

00:36:08.429 --> 00:36:10.948
Goodbye Sam.

00:36:15.014 --> 00:36:16.700
Mrs. Roke.

00:36:16.735 --> 00:36:18.909
You pray with me now.

00:36:18.944 --> 00:36:21.084
Pray with me friends.

00:36:50.225 --> 00:36:52.298
All right now.

00:36:53.361 --> 00:36:56.187
All right now.

00:37:21.927 --> 00:37:23.857
All right.

00:37:49.370 --> 00:37:54.587
I don't understand. I
don't feel different.

00:37:55.425 --> 00:37:56.495
My god!

00:37:56.530 --> 00:37:58.449
What have you done?

00:37:58.484 --> 00:38:00.368
He's not your god.

00:38:00.403 --> 00:38:02.407
Reverend?

00:38:02.442 --> 00:38:04.412
Sue Ann?

00:38:50.727 --> 00:38:52.444
You okay?

00:38:52.732 --> 00:38:54.801
A little bit weak.

00:38:54.836 --> 00:38:56.472
Yeah.

00:38:57.674 --> 00:38:59.534
All right, come on.

00:38:59.569 --> 00:39:01.394
We should get going.

00:39:12.740 --> 00:39:14.834
What is it?

00:39:14.869 --> 00:39:16.928
Nothing.

00:39:18.307 --> 00:39:19.585
What is it?

00:39:19.620 --> 00:39:21.550
We did the right thing here, didn't' we?

00:39:21.585 --> 00:39:23.618
Of course we did.

00:39:23.653 --> 00:39:25.975
I didn't feel like it.

00:39:27.073 --> 00:39:28.784
I got it.

00:39:32.610 --> 00:39:36.005
Leila, come on in. Hey.

00:39:36.040 --> 00:39:37.916
Hey.

00:39:38.762 --> 00:39:40.570
How did you know we were here?

00:39:40.605 --> 00:39:42.461
Sam called.

00:39:42.496 --> 00:39:46.242
He said you wanted to say goodbye.

00:39:46.409 --> 00:39:49.423
I'm gonna grab a soda.

00:39:54.143 --> 00:39:56.268
So um...

00:39:56.303 --> 00:39:59.484
Where are you going?

00:39:59.519 --> 00:40:00.690
Don't know yet.

00:40:00.725 --> 00:40:04.769
Our work kind of takes us all over so...

00:40:06.499 --> 00:40:10.863
You know, I went back to see Roy.

00:40:10.898 --> 00:40:13.527
What happened?

00:40:14.756 --> 00:40:17.068
Nothing.

00:40:17.290 --> 00:40:23.313
He laid his hand on my
forehead. But nothing happened.

00:40:23.348 --> 00:40:25.907
I'm sorry.

00:40:26.091 --> 00:40:28.670
I'm sorry it didn't work.

00:40:28.705 --> 00:40:30.642
And Sue Ann...

00:40:30.677 --> 00:40:32.342
She's dead, you know?

00:40:32.377 --> 00:40:34.292
A stroke.

00:40:34.327 --> 00:40:37.411
Yeah, I heard.

00:40:38.068 --> 00:40:41.210
Yeah, Roy's a good man.

00:40:41.383 --> 00:40:44.614
He doesn't deserve what's happened.

00:40:47.500 --> 00:40:49.845
Must be ruff...

00:40:49.880 --> 00:40:52.250
To believe in something so much.

00:40:52.285 --> 00:40:55.665
And have it disappoint you like that.

00:40:59.801 --> 00:41:03.103
You want to hear something weird?

00:41:04.304 --> 00:41:09.131
I'm okay. Really.

00:41:09.166 --> 00:41:11.525
I guess if you're gonna have faith

00:41:11.560 --> 00:41:14.703
We can't just have it
when the miracles happen.

00:41:14.738 --> 00:41:19.978
You have to have it when they don't.

00:41:24.628 --> 00:41:28.077
So what now?

00:41:30.489 --> 00:41:34.977
God works in mysterious ways.

00:41:39.107 --> 00:41:41.479
Goodbye Dean.

00:41:43.207 --> 00:41:44.923
Hey.

00:41:50.176 --> 00:41:55.269
I'm not much of a praying type but...

00:41:56.137 --> 00:41:59.611
I'm gonna pray for you.

00:42:00.769 --> 00:42:03.118
Well...

00:42:03.284 --> 00:42:06.769
There's a miracle right there.



00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
